"""The I-8 master evaluation set: real-knowledge-base questions for the full end-to-end QA of the integrated runtime
(runtime integration, phase I-8). Every entry records the domain the question belongs to, its test category, tags, the
behaviour a correct runtime may show and the handbook fact it rests on (printed page of the UOS Faculty Handbook 2025/26).

``expect`` says what a CORRECT runtime may do, never what it does:
    serve     the handbook states the asked fact specifically; a served answer is desirable (a fallback is a coverage gap)
    fallback  Plan F must not serve: the premise is false, the subject or condition is not in the handbook, the ask is
              general, enumerative, comparative or needs synthesis (a served answer is a false acceptance)
    either    serving the verbatim statement or falling back are both acceptable; a served answer must still be correct

Regression questions carry the ``regression`` tag and keep the exact wording of the earlier corpora (qa/plan_f_i3 to i6).
"""

